  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5257",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the pathogenesis of LB771-HNC through a shared target, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which acts as a modulator of P2X purinoceptors. This compound is identified as a target of Mollicellin N, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of P2X receptors. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Mollicellin N may exert its effects by targeting P2X receptors, which are known to play a role in cellular signaling and may contribute to the pathophysiology of LB771-HNC. The consistent involvement of the same compound in the targeting of P2X receptors across different paths strengthens the hypothesis that Mollicellin N interacts with these receptors to influence the disease state. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a well-documented target relationship, and the evidence suggests a direct, mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and LB771-HNC through the modulation of P2X purinoceptors.",
